/*
  MetricCard.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0095 · MetricCard (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web `MetricCard`
  (components/data-display/MetricCard.tsx) is itself anonymous — its visible label / value / subtitle
  / change-pill text are all caller-supplied and are NOT translated copy (the web renders them
  verbatim), so they carry no keys here. The user-facing COPY the card resolves comes from the two
  atomic components it composes — `<HelpTooltip>` and `<Delta>` — through the same `t()` keys the web
  uses, mirrored here so the inline native reproduction holds no hardcoded prose:

    • metricCard.help.ariaLabel — the help "?" trigger's VoiceOver label. The web uses the literal
                                  template `More info about ${label}`; localized here as a positional
                                  `%1$@` format (an improvement over the web literal).
    • common.learnMore          — the help popover's "Learn more" link (web HelpTooltip
                                  `t('common.learnMore', 'Learn more')`).
    • delta.title               — the populated delta's VoiceOver title (web Delta
                                  `t('delta.title', '{{current}} vs {{previous}}')`). `%1$@` / `%2$@`
                                  are the formatted endpoints, positional so a translation may reorder.
    • delta.noComparison        — the empty delta's label (web Delta
                                  `t('delta.noComparison', 'No comparison data')`).

  These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are
  kept in a per-surface table ("MetricCard") so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings.
*/

/* --- Help affordance (web HelpTooltip) --- */
"metricCard.help.ariaLabel" = "More info about %1$@";
"common.learnMore" = "Learn more";

/* --- Delta footer (web Delta) --- */
"delta.title" = "%1$@ vs %2$@";
"delta.noComparison" = "No comparison data";
